&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family:calibri,calibri_embeddedfont,calibri_msfontservice,sans-serif; font-size:12pt"&gt;The Network for Oregon Affordable Housing (NOAH) is a nonprofit community development financial institution (CDFI) that provides financing for the development and preservation of affordable housing throughout Oregon. Formed in 1990 to increase the supply of safe, healthy, and stable housing, NOAH now administers over $400 million of loan capital through a growing array of loan programs to support the preservation and development of new affordable housing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
