&lt;p style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:20px"&gt;2025 in Review: Job Losses and Rising Unemployment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:16px"&gt;Oregon&rsquo;s labor force grows slightly despite negative turn in job growth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SALEM, Ore&lt;/strong&gt;. &mdash;&amp;nbsp;Oregon saw job growth in a handful of sectors and experienced a small increase in its labor force, but overall, the state lost jobs in 2025 as the unemployment rate rose nearly a point to 5.2%.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;a href="https://qualityinfo.org/-/job-losses-and-rising-unemployment-2025-in-review"&gt;reviewing the year&lt;/a&gt;, state employment economist Gail Krumenauer noted job gains were concentrated in private health care and social assistance, but rising jobless workers resulted in the highest unemployment rate &ndash; outside a recession or recovery period &ndash; in a decade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looking ahead, Oregon&rsquo;s Office of Economic Analysis expects a rebound to slow job gains in 2026.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Visit &lt;a href="https://www.qualityinfo.org/"&gt;QualityInfo.org&lt;/a&gt; for the full &lt;a href="https://qualityinfo.org/-/job-losses-and-rising-unemployment-2025-in-review"&gt;Year in Review&lt;/a&gt; article.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;
